
# 6. SRS — SOFTWARE REQUIREMENTS SPECIFICATION

# FixMyCampus — Software Requirements Specification

**Version:** 1.0
**Date:** 06 September 2026

---

# 1. Introduction

## 1.1 Purpose

This Software Requirements Specification defines the functional and non-functional requirements of the FixMyCampus web application.

It serves as a reference for:

* Development
* Testing
* Demonstration
* Academic evaluation
* Maintenance

---

# 1.2 Scope

The software provides:

* User registration
* Authentication
* Role-based dashboards
* Complaint creation
* Complaint tracking
* Admin assignment
* Staff processing
* Status updates
* Complaint timeline
* Notifications
* Complaint-specific chat
* Student closure
* Feedback
* XML export
* XSD validation
* DTD validation

---

# 2. Overall Description

## 2.1 Product Perspective

FixMyCampus is a standalone web application.

Its architecture is:

```text
User Browser
     ↓
HTML / CSS / JavaScript
     ↓
PHP Backend
     ↓
MySQL Database
```

XML processing operates alongside the application backend.

---

# 2.2 Product Functions

The major functions are:

1. Registration
2. Login
3. Logout
4. Complaint creation
5. Complaint listing
6. Complaint details
7. Complaint assignment
8. Staff processing
9. Status updates
10. Resolution
11. Student closure
12. Notifications
13. Chat
14. Feedback
15. XML export
16. XSD validation
17. DTD validation

---

# 3. Functional Requirements

## FR-01 — Authentication

The system shall authenticate registered users and create a server-side session.

---

## FR-02 — Authorization

The system shall enforce role-based permissions for:

```text
Student
Staff
Admin
```

---

## FR-03 — Registration

The system shall allow users to register using required account information.

Passwords shall be stored securely using password hashing.

---

## FR-04 — Complaint Creation

The system shall allow students to create complaints containing:

* Category
* Location
* Title
* Description
* Priority

The system shall generate a unique complaint code.

---

## FR-05 — Complaint Ownership

The system shall ensure that students can retrieve only their own complaints.

---

## FR-06 — Admin Review

The system shall allow administrators to view complaints across the system.

---

## FR-07 — Staff Assignment

The system shall allow administrators to assign complaints to staff.

---

## FR-08 — Staff Queue

The system shall show staff only complaints currently assigned to them.

---

## FR-09 — Status Update

The system shall allow assigned staff to update complaint status and provide remarks.

---

## FR-10 — Resolution Timestamp

When staff marks a complaint as:

```text
Resolved
```

the server shall record:

```text
resolved_at
```

---

## FR-11 — Student Closure

The system shall allow the complaint owner to close a complaint only when:

```text
status = Resolved
```

---

## FR-12 — Closure Timestamp

When the student successfully closes the complaint, the server shall record:

```text
closed_at
```

---

## FR-13 — Complaint Timeline

The system shall record status changes and remarks in:

```text
complaint_updates
```

---

## FR-14 — Chat Authorization

The system shall allow complaint chat only to:

```text
Complaint Owner
```

or

```text
Currently Assigned Staff
```

---

## FR-15 — Closed Chat

The system shall:

* Allow historical messages to be viewed.
* Reject new messages after complaint closure.

The restriction must be enforced server-side.

---

## FR-16 — Notifications

The system shall create notifications for relevant complaint events.

Notifications shall support:

* Read
* Unread
* Mark individual as read
* Mark all as read

---

## FR-17 — Feedback

The system shall allow students to submit feedback after complaint closure.

The rating shall be between:

```text
1 and 5
```

A complaint can have one feedback record.

---

## FR-18 — XML Export

The system shall generate complaint information in XML format.

Authorized students can export their own complaints.

Administrators can export authorized complaint information.

---

## FR-19 — XSD Validation

The system shall validate complaint XML against:

```text
complaint.xsd
```

---

## FR-20 — DTD Validation

The system shall validate complaint XML against:

```text
complaint.dtd
```

---

# 4. Data Requirements

## User

The user entity contains:

* User ID
* Name
* Email
* Phone
* Password
* Role
* Status
* Created timestamp

---

## Complaint

The complaint entity contains:

* Complaint ID
* Complaint code
* Student
* Category
* Location
* Title
* Description
* Priority
* Status
* Created timestamp
* Updated timestamp
* Resolved timestamp
* Closed timestamp

---

## Complaint Update

Contains:

* Update ID
* Complaint
* User
* Old status
* New status
* Remarks
* Updated timestamp

---

## Staff Assignment

Contains:

* Assignment ID
* Complaint
* Staff
* Assigning admin
* Assignment timestamp
* Completion timestamp

---

## Message

Contains:

* Message ID
* Complaint
* Sender
* Message
* Created timestamp
* Read status

---

## Notification

Contains:

* Notification ID
* User
* Complaint
* Message
* Read status
* Created timestamp

---

## Feedback

Contains:

* Feedback ID
* Complaint
* Student
* Rating
* Comment
* Created timestamp

---

# 5. Non-Functional Requirements

## 5.1 Security

The system shall enforce:

* Authentication
* Authorization
* Ownership validation
* Staff assignment validation
* Chat authorization
* Closure authorization

---

## 5.2 Performance

Normal application operations should return promptly for the intended academic/demo dataset and local deployment environment.

---

## 5.3 Usability

The system shall provide role-specific interfaces.

Students should see student functions.

Staff should see staff functions.

Administrators should see administrative functions.

---

## 5.4 Maintainability

The project shall maintain separation between:

```text
HTML
CSS
JavaScript
PHP
Database
XML
```

---

## 5.5 Reliability

Database constraints and server-side validation should preserve complaint consistency.

---

## 5.6 Compatibility

The system shall support modern desktop web browsers in the target local environment.

---

## 5.7 Auditability

Complaint status changes shall be stored in the complaint update history.

---

# 6. Use Case Summary

| Use Case          | Actor           | Result                     |
| ----------------- | --------------- | -------------------------- |
| Register          | User            | Account created            |
| Login             | User            | Session established        |
| Report Complaint  | Student         | Complaint created          |
| View Complaint    | Student         | Own complaint displayed    |
| Assign Complaint  | Admin           | Staff assigned             |
| Process Complaint | Staff           | Status updated             |
| Resolve Complaint | Staff           | Complaint becomes Resolved |
| Close Complaint   | Student         | Complaint becomes Closed   |
| Chat              | Student/Staff   | Complaint communication    |
| Feedback          | Student         | Feedback stored            |
| Export XML        | Student/Admin   | XML generated              |
| Validate XML      | Authorized User | XSD/DTD results displayed  |

